            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0341" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 18071/6–9.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 166.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your No. 223, of February 24
                    last, and with reference to the department’s No. 106, of the 5th of that month,
                    relative to the military-service case of Mr. Gottlob Blickle, a naturalized
                    citizen of the United States of German birth, I now inclose the form of
                    statement forwarded by the embassy wherein Mr. Blickle furnishes the information
                    required by the German authorities before consideration can be given his
                    case.</p>
                <p>Mr. Blickle’s German passport is also inclosed for the use of the embassy.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
